# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
# NOTE: NO backticks and NO dollar-sign in the desc/blurb text below (shell-eval fragility -- see CLAUDE.md).
register_gate "tests/test_suspend_handler.py" "SUSPEND HANDLER GATE: PASS" "installation.suspend is HANDLED (non-noop suspended verdict + account-wide lane quiesce), not silently dropped" "Unhandled installation.suspend (MED lifecycle -- same class as the round-4 unhandled-lifecycle-event HIGH, lower blast radius): the GitHub webhook action installation.suspend was UNHANDLED. handle_event (github-app/webhook_handlers.py) branched only on created / unsuspend / new_permissions_accepted (onboard) and deleted (purge); suspend matched NO branch so it fell through to the generic noop, and event_processor._INSTALL_FANOUT_FIELD had no suspend entry. OBSERVED HARM (reproduced empirically): after a suspend was delivered the account's in-flight lanes stayed HELD (Veripsa released nothing -- correct behavior depended ENTIRELY on GitHub's external masking, which does NOT cover at-least-once REDELIVERY of a queued event nor the rolling-deploy 2-instance overlap during the suspend transition), AND a subsequent pull_request for that account was STILL fully processed (it posted a check AND acquired a new active claim, count 0->1). unsuspend already re-onboards (resume covered); only suspend was the hole. THE FIX (minimal, content-free, advisory): (a) handle_event handles installation.suspend EXPLICITLY -- returns a non-noop suspended verdict and releases the account's in-flight lanes ACCOUNT-WIDE via core.release_account_claims_with_authority (the graph-preserving counterpart to the repo archived release; NOT the uninstall purge -- suspend is REVERSIBLE, so the code graph + the append-only event ledger are KEPT and unsuspend re-onboards from the retained structure); (b) a SUSPEND-WINDOW QUIESCE at the top of handle_event -- any WORK-bearing event (pull_request / push / ...) delivered while the install is suspended (GitHub stamps installation.suspended_at on it, a content-free timestamp) is a clean no-op (no lane, no check); the lifecycle events installation / installation_repositories are exempt (they carry their own correct handling -- suspend RELEASES, unsuspend RE-ONBOARDS, deleted PURGES -- and the suspend payload itself carries suspended_at, so a blanket top-level skip would short-circuit the very release); (c) a minimal account-scoped release fn release_account_claims_with_authority (35_lifecycle.sql) mirroring release_repo_claims_with_authority but account-wide, App-delegation only (veripsa_app; REVOKEd from PUBLIC + veripsa_writer), identity from the connection role (no tenant arg -> no cross-tenant release), graph kept, no waiter promoted (the whole account lane namespace is emptied). suspend is DELIBERATELY not fanned out per-repo (same shape as deleted -- it is account-wide). WHAT THIS GATE PROVES (driven through the REAL make_db_processor / handle_event over the REAL gate, authed as the REAL least-privilege role veripsa_app, against a scratch Postgres -- the exact prod transaction model): (1) installation.suspend returns a clear suspended verdict, NOT a noop (origin/main returns noop true -> FAILS); (2) an account that held an in-flight lane has it RELEASED by the suspend (active/waiting claims go to 0; origin/main leaves it held -> FAILS); (3) a pull_request delivered DURING the suspend window (carrying installation.suspended_at) acquires NO new active lane and posts NO check (origin/main fully processes it, claim 0->1 + check posted -> FAILS); (4) a later unsuspend STILL re-onboards (its graph is re-ingested + committed -- the resume path is intact, no regression). Content-free throughout (a suspended_at timestamp + repo full_names + claim-count / committed-graph readbacks, never bodies); advisory + fail-safe unchanged (a malformed payload has no suspended_at -> not skipped)." 12
